// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - MarchandClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4234855970" "Marchand's Orders"
// DetailString :
"P621750059" "Provost Marchand has given you very specific orders: stop the plan to blow up Enriche and arrest Calvin Scott for all of his crimes."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - DarkWatcherMoralChoice 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef Name :
"P738223855" "Empty Bottle of Enriche"
// tDetailString :
"P3531316488" "You picked up this empty bottle of Enriche in the main Enriche factory in Neutropolis. It reminds you of an experience called...<br><br><color Paragon>To Our Health</color><br><br>Dark Watcher had one last task for you after you thwarted Cole's plans for an invasion. He asked that you go down to help Calvin Scott blow up the main source of Enriche in Praetoria. However, this would mean the people of Praetoria would be left with sick and diseased water for at least five months. Were you willing to have the people suffer for their freedom and the help of Vanguard, or did you move to stop Scott's plans in the hopes of finding a better one that did not involve the risk of people's health?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Marchand 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1049807587" "{HeroName}, what is your current situation?"
// Answer Text :
"P109192126" "(Explain the situation with Scott and Enriche)"
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P523431731" "This is the perfect opportunity for us, {HeroName}. We need to ensure that Enriche is kept safe for the people. The loss of it would cause too much sickness and disease in Praetoria.<br><br>Ensure that it is truly just you and Scott. When the opportunity presents itself, <i>bring in Calvin Scott</i>. I want him alive, {HeroName}. He's going to answer for all the people that he's hurt for his cause."
// Answer Text :
"P4250498222" "I understand, Marchand."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Scott 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2881193312" "{HeroName}? Are you going to arm the bombs? I thought I made it - <br><br><color orange>Calvin Scott stares at you, his one eye widening in awareness.</color><br><br>So, you're not going to help. You don't believe that this is a worthy cause? Do you feel this is going too far, that we <i>shouldn't</i> destroy Enriche?"
// Answer Text :
"P1603962399" "The cost is too high Scott. There has to be another way. We have time now."
// Answer Text :
"P2524526289" "Actually, Scott. I've been working to undermine the Resistance all this time."
// Page Page2 Text :
"P1798332409" "Don't you understand? There <i>is</i> no other way. This is <i>the</i> only way to bring Enriche and Cole down!<br><br>Freedom isn't easy, {HeroName}, it's going to come with suffering. If you can't accept that, then I'll just have to do this on my own. I'm not going to let someone who is as weak-willed as <i>you</i> get in the way of our victory over Cole!"
// Answer Text :
"P4211051699" "I won't let you do this, Scott!"
// Page Page3 Text :
"P2367840861" "You don't have a choice, {HeroName}!"
// Answer Text :
"P403194582" "(Fight Scott!)"
// Page MarchandSpy Text :
"P1251853794" "<color orange>Calvin Scott's fists clench as he cracks his neck.</color><br><br>How long have you been acting as a spy, {HeroName}? No... I don't believe it matters at this point. You and I are here now, just the two of us. This would, in all cases, appear to be exactly where you want me.<br><br>But ask yourself this, {HeroName}. Do you think you're the first person to betray me? The first Loyalist to try to work undercover to bring me down?"
// Answer Text :
"P572603875" "No. But I'm going to be the last."
// Page Marchand2 Text :
"P2594106647" "We'll see about that!"
// Answer Text :
"P70352629" "You won't get away, Scott!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2073881900" "We've struck a blow against Cole's invasion, but now we must move quickly to strike another. I am sure you're aware of the ever looming presence of <color yellow>Enriche</color>, are you not? I am sure you're aware that this is no normal water. There are special chemicals within Enriche that help to placate the people, make them less suspicious of goings on. This is why there can be outbreaks of monsters in Neutropolis and the people simply take the word of the PPD or Berry that they will address the situation at hand.<br><br>It will make things rather difficult for our allies to fight Cole if he still has the support of the people. I shall be honest and upfront with you, {HeroName}. I am part of an organization called Vanguard. We handle inter-dimensional threats. The head of it, Lady Grey, has stated that Vanguard only has the resources to fight one war against Emperor Cole, and that is a war of combat. We do not have the time to also fight a war of public relations. It is because of this that we must get to the center of Enriche and destroy it. But, you will have help."
// AcceptString :
"P2387470853" "Who is going to help me?"
// SendOffString :
"P2536173170" "<color yellow>Calvin Scott himself.</color> We have discovered a way into the main water pumping station for the Enriche chemicals. Meet with Calvin Scott and do what you can to give him the support he needs. Once Enriche is destroyed, I will be able to have Vanguard move in its supplies. I estimate the people here in Praetoria will have to go for about <color yellow>five to six months</color> with unclean and impure water. This is just the nature of things, you see. The Enriche factory is the main, and last, source of clean water in Praetoria, due to all the fallout from the Hamidon Wars. However, once Vanguard has established a base of operations in the tunnels, we will be able to give the people clean and proper water and give medical support for anyone who has become severely injured during this time.<br><br><color gold>Those Loyalists working undercover for Provost Marchand should speak to him about these events.</color>"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3643465556" "Destroy Enriche (Single Player)"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P988387602" "Scott is waiting, {HeroName}."
// TaskTitle :
"P3610989358" "<color deepskyblue>To Our Health</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P2548791158" "<color deepskyblue>Finale: The People's Minds, the People's Health</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P318905560" "Calvin Scott, the leader of the Resistance, is up ahead in the tunnels, waiting for you."

